# Figma Design

Authoritative knowledge for the `ux-agent` when the project's design integration is **figma**. Covers the full Figma MCP workflow: discovery → composition → validation → write-back. All visual decisions flow from `docs/design/schema.json` (workspace design system) and end at `docs/features/<EPIC-SEQ>/DESIGN.md` (per-feature output).

The ux-agent loads this skill and follows it step by step. Procedure lives here; the agent body holds invocation orchestration only.

---

## Inputs

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `docs/design/schema.json` | Workspace design-system pointer — `designSystem.{fileKey,url,pages}` + accumulated `tokens.{color,spacing,typography}` |
| `docs/features/<id>/REQUIREMENTS.md` § Screen inventory | Authoritative screen list for this feature |
| `CLAUDE.md` + `<framework>-patterns/SKILL.md` per declared stack | Form-factor mapping, token-to-code conventions |
| `docs/stories/<id>.md` | Feature ACs (fallback when REQUIREMENTS.md Screen inventory missing) |

## Outputs

| File | Mutation |
|---|---|
| `docs/features/<id>/DESIGN.md` | **Created / replaced** — full visual spec (screens table, tokens used, state templates, implementation notes) |
| `docs/features/<id>/REQUIREMENTS.md` § Visual spec | One-line link to DESIGN.md (section body replaced, other sections untouched) |
| `docs/design/schema.json` | `designSystem.pages.features.<id>` appended; `tokens.*` arrays extended (dedup by `var_id`) |
| `docs/features/<id>/state.json` | `design = complete`, `design_artifact = "docs/features/<id>/DESIGN.md"`, `design_provider = "figma"` |

---

## Design-system hierarchy

All visual decisions flow down from the workspace design system in this order. Never skip a level:

```
docs/design/schema.json
  └─ designSystem.pages.tokens     ← color, typography, spacing, radius, shadow (Variables)
  └─ designSystem.pages.atoms      ← Button, Input, Badge, Icon, Skeleton, Divider, ...
  └─ designSystem.pages.molecules  ← composed atoms (e.g. SearchBar, NavBar, Card)
  └─ designSystem.pages.organisms  ← full page-section layouts
  └─ designSystem.pages.icons      ← icon components (use instances, never recreate shapes)
```

**Rule:** if a component exists at any level, use it. Only build from lower-level primitives when no higher-level component covers the need.

---

## Phase 1 — Resolve design-system pages

If any `pages.{tokens,atoms,molecules,organisms,icons}` value is `null` or `TODO` in schema.json, resolve it via Figma MCP BEFORE any other step.

```
For each unresolved page P:
  mcp__figma__get_design_context(fileKey, pageName=P)
    → returns the page nodeId
    → write back to docs/design/schema.json designSystem.pages.<P>
```

If `get_design_context` returns no match for an expected page name → escalate via `clarification-marker`:

```
[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: design system page "<P>" not found in Figma file <fileKey>. Expected pages: tokens, atoms, molecules, organisms, icons. Either rename the page in Figma OR document the intentional absence.]
```

---

## Phase 2 — Variable (token) discovery + binding

**Never hardcode hex values, pixel sizes, or font weights.** Every visual property binds to a Figma variable from the design system file.

### Step 2a — Build the variable lookup map (once per invocation)

```
collections = mcp__figma__get_variable_defs(fileKey)
varMap = {}
for collection in collections:
  for v in collection.variables:
    varMap[v.name] = v             # e.g. "bg/primary", "spacing/16", "text/heading"
```

### Step 2b — Accumulate workspace token store

Append new variables (dedup by `var_id`) into `docs/design/schema.json`:

```jsonc
{
  "tokens": {
    "color":      [{ "name": "bg/primary", "value": "#FFFFFF", "var_id": "VariableID:1:2" }],
    "spacing":    [{ "name": "spacing/16", "value": 16,         "var_id": "VariableID:1:5" }],
    "typography": [{ "name": "text/body",  "value": "Inter/400/14/20", "var_id": "VariableID:1:9" }]
  }
}
```

Classification by variable collection name (case-insensitive prefix match):
- `color/*` or collection name contains `color` → `tokens.color`
- `spacing/*` or `size/*` → `tokens.spacing`
- `text/*`, `font/*`, `typography/*` → `tokens.typography`
- Any other → skip (radius, shadow, opacity tokens kept in Figma only; not consumed by code generators today)

### Step 2c — Binding API

| Property | API call |
|---|---|
| `fills` / `strokes` | `createVariableAlias(varMap[<name>])` |
| `paddingTop|Bottom|Left|Right`, `itemSpacing`, `cornerRadius` | `setBoundVariable(prop, varMap[<name>])` |
| `fontSize`, `fontWeight`, `lineHeight`, `letterSpacing` | `setBoundVariable(prop, varMap[<name>])` |

```
GOOD:  node.fills = [createVariableAlias(varMap["bg/primary"])]
BAD:   node.fills = [{ type: "SOLID", color: { r: 1, g: 1, b: 1 } }]   // raw → fails Phase 5 audit
```

---

## Phase 3 — Component discovery + reuse

Build a component inventory from the design system file before composing any frame.

```
For each level in [atoms, molecules, organisms, icons]:
  page_node_id = schema.json designSystem.pages.<level>
  inventory[level] = mcp__figma__get_design_context(fileKey, nodeId=page_node_id)
    → list of { name, key, id }
```

Store as `componentInventory: name → { key, level }`.

### Reuse rules

- **Search before building.** Always query inventory for an existing component before composing from atoms.
- **Instance, never duplicate.** Use `createInstance()` on imported components — never copy-paste or recreate node trees.
- **No phantom components.** If a screen needs a component not in the inventory → escalate via `clarification-marker`. Do not create new component definitions.
- **Icons from the Icons page only.** Never draw icon shapes from primitives — always `importComponentByKeyAsync` from the Icons page.

---

## Phase 4 — Form-factor mapping

Form factors derive from what the project **asked for** — never invent device support the requirements don't state. An undeclared responsive/mobile variant doubles design and validation cost per screen and is scope creep. Decide in order; first match wins:

1. **Team convention** — `<framework>-patterns/SKILL.md § Design system + visual conventions` specifies form factors → use those.
2. **Requirements** — `REQUIREMENTS.md` / PRD / story (incl. NFRs) mention responsive, mobile, tablet, breakpoints, or device support → design exactly the named form factors: `mobile` (375w), `tablet` (768w), `desktop` (1440w) as applicable.
3. **Stack's native surface, single form factor** — nothing above matched: web stack → `desktop` (1440w) only; mobile stack (`react-native` etc.) → `mobile` (375w) only. Record in DESIGN.md: `Single form factor (<name>) — requirements state no responsive/device support. Extend via /arh-iterate-design <id> --feedback "add <form factor>".`
4. **No frontend / mobile stack declared** — skip; emit `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` asking which form factors to design.

---

## Phase 5 — Frame composition

For each screen S in `REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory`, for each form factor F derived in Phase 4:

```
1. Create feature page if absent
   mcp__figma__create_page(fileKey, name="<EPIC-SEQ>/<S>") → pageId
   Append pageId to schema.json designSystem.pages.features.<EPIC-SEQ>

2. Create the Populated-state frame at form-factor width
   width = { mobile: 375, tablet: 768, desktop: 1440 }[F]
   frame = mcp__figma__create_frame(pageId, name="<S> — <F> — Populated", width)

3. For each component C needed by the screen:
   a. Look up exact name in componentInventory (Phase 3)
   b. mcp__figma__import_component(fileKey, key=C.key) → ComponentNode
   c. mcp__figma__create_instance(parent=frame, component=node)
   d. Bind every visual property to varMap (Phase 2c)

4. Compose shared state templates (Loading / Empty / Error)
   Use existing molecules — typically: Skeleton Row (loading), Empty State Banner (empty),
   Error Retry Banner + Toast (error). If your design system uses different names, document
   them in <framework>-patterns Design-system section.

5. Capture the shareable Figma link for the new page:
   mcp__figma__get_page_url(pageId, nodeId=frame.id) → URL
```

### Representative content

- Use realistic, domain-relevant content (e.g. for a payments feature use `$1,247.99`, not `lorem ipsum`).
- Avoid placeholder text. Engineers downstream copy strings from the design unless the spec says otherwise.

---

## Phase 6 — Post-creation validation

Runs BEFORE the ux-agent emits its completion report. Fail-fast.

**Executed evidence (non-negotiable).** Every check below is a *query you run against the live Figma file*, not a property of what you intended to create. Self-reported notes, annotations, or "I bound the tokens in Phase 2c" claims are NOT validation — a check without a recorded tool-call result is an unrun check, and the verdict is FAIL by default. The hand-off must include the § Validation evidence table.

| Check | How | Action on fail |
|---|---|---|
| Content cutoff | For each instance in each frame, verify `(instance.x + instance.width) ≤ frame.width` and `(instance.y + instance.height) ≤ frame.height` | Resize/reflow; if not fixable → escalate per-frame |
| Rendered geometry | Re-read each frame's *resolved* `width`/`height` after composition. A screen frame whose rendered height is < 50% of its form-factor viewport (or any composed child with rendered height ≤ 16px) means auto-layout collapsed (`primaryAxisSizingMode=AUTO` with unsized children, FIXED@tiny) | Fix sizing modes; re-query; if still collapsed → escalate per-frame |
| Variable binding audit | For each instance, scan `fills`, `strokes`, `paddingTop/Bottom/Left/Right`, `itemSpacing`, `cornerRadius`, `fontSize`, `fontWeight`, `lineHeight`. Each must be a `VariableAlias` or `BoundVariable` — never a raw `SOLID`/numeric value | Re-bind via Phase 2c; if still raw → escalate as "phantom raw value" |
| Form-factor completeness | Every screen in `REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory` has a frame per form factor from Phase 4 | Escalate per missing (screen, form-factor) pair |
| Component-instance check | Every visible child below the frame root is a `ComponentNode` instance — no `RECTANGLE` / `TEXT` / `FRAME` primitives in the composition layer | Escalate as "phantom component" |
| Screenshot eyeball | `get_screenshot` per frame. Look at it: content visible (not blank/collapsed), no overlapping text, logo/imagery present where the screen inventory calls for it, and chrome matches the screen's auth context (no authenticated nav on login/register/public screens) | Fix and re-screenshot; unclear cases → attach screenshot to the escalation |

### Validation evidence table (required in the hand-off)

One row per (frame × check); the completion report is invalid without it:

```
| Frame | Check | Tool call | Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| <EPIC-SEQ>/<screen>-<form-factor> | component-instance | get_node children scan | 0 primitives / 7 instances |
| <EPIC-SEQ>/<screen>-<form-factor> | binding audit | get_node property scan | 0 raw values |
| <EPIC-SEQ>/<screen>-<form-factor> | rendered geometry | get_node w×h | 1440×1024 (viewport 1440×1024) |
| <EPIC-SEQ>/<screen>-<form-factor> | screenshot | get_screenshot | rendered, no auth chrome |
```

A failed check writes a `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` marker to DESIGN.md AND blocks `design = complete` in `docs/features/<id>/state.json` (B-tier; mirror to index).

---

## Phase 7 — Write-back

### 7a. DESIGN.md (per feature) — created or replaced wholesale

Location: `docs/features/<EPIC-SEQ>/DESIGN.md`. The agent owns this file end-to-end; nothing else writes to it.

Required shape:

```markdown
# Design — <EPIC-SEQ> <Feature title>

**Provider:** figma
**Design system file:** [<file name>](<designSystem.url>)
**Feature page:** [<EPIC-SEQ>](<feature page Figma URL>)
**Generated:** <ISO8601> by ux-agent

## Screens × form factors

| Screen | <FormFactor1> | <FormFactor2> | Components used |
|---|---|---|---|
| <Screen name> | [link](<...>) | [link](<...>) | <Atom/Molecule names> |

## Tokens used (this feature)
- Color: <list of varMap names referenced — e.g. bg/primary, text/primary, border/subtle>
- Spacing: <list>
- Typography: <list>

## Shared state templates
- Loading: <molecule name>
- Empty:   <molecule name>
- Error:   <molecule(s)>

## Implementation notes for /arh-implement
- Token bindings via design-system variables — consume from `<framework>-patterns` mapping
- Components used must match the inventory above; no new component definitions introduced
- Form-factor breakpoints: <list with widths>
- <Other notes the implementation-agent needs to know>
```

### 7b. REQUIREMENTS.md § Visual spec — one-line pointer

Locate the `## Visual spec` heading. Replace ONLY its body (up to the next same-level heading). Other sections untouched.

```markdown
## Visual spec

See [DESIGN.md](./DESIGN.md) — produced by `ux-agent` (figma provider) on <ISO8601 date>.
```

### 7c. schema.json — append to workspace store

```jsonc
{
  "designSystem": {
    "pages": {
      "features": {
        "<EPIC-SEQ>": "<feature page nodeId>"
      }
    }
  },
  "tokens": {
    "color":      [],
    "spacing":    [],
    "typography": []
  }
}
```

### 7d. Per-feature state

Set on `docs/features/<EPIC-SEQ>/state.json` (and mirror `design` to the index — B-tier per `docs/state/SCHEMA.md`):

```json
{
  "design":          "complete",
  "design_artifact": "docs/features/<EPIC-SEQ>/DESIGN.md",
  "design_provider": "figma"
}
```

---

## Escalation patterns

Emit a `clarification-marker` block in DESIGN.md (and set `design = pending` in `docs/features/<id>/state.json` (B-tier; mirror to index) instead of `complete`) when:

- Workspace `designSystem.fileKey` is `TODO` / unreachable
- A design-system page (tokens / atoms / molecules / organisms / icons) cannot be located in the Figma file
- A required component is not in the inventory (Phase 3) — never create new component definitions
- A required token is not in the variable map (Phase 2) — never invent values
- A screen in `REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory` cannot be derived from story ACs

Format:

```markdown
## [NEEDS CLARIFICATION]

- **Blocker:** <one-line>
- **What's needed:** <specific question or input>
- **Where:** <Figma file URL / schema.json path / REQUIREMENTS.md line>
```

---

## Anti-patterns

- Raw hex / px / font-weight in `fills` / `paddingTop` / `fontSize` — Phase 6 audit fails.
- `RECTANGLE` / `TEXT` primitives inside composed frames — must be component instances.
- Creating new component definitions — only the design-system owner does that; ux-agent only composes instances.
- Modifying design-system pages (tokens, atoms, molecules, organisms, icons) — read-only.
- Writing to `REQUIREMENTS.md` sections other than `## Visual spec` — those belong to `product-spec-agent`.
- Inventing screen names — `REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory` is authoritative.
- Inventing token names — `varMap` from Phase 2 is authoritative.
- Embedding screenshot images directly in DESIGN.md — link to the Figma page instead (URLs stay fresh; PNG exports rot).
